          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: A motorist and his passenger on the A6 highway were surprised to observe, twice, a stationary luminous phenomenon in the sky at approximately 30° above the horizon. The phenomenon suddenly disappeared without leaving a trace. With a low strangeness rating but relatively precise details, this observation is classified as a probable reflection of the sun on high-altitude aircraft. This case is classified B.",
